          "source_quote": "τῷ ἐν εἱρκτῇ κατὰ τὸ δυνατὸν ἐπιραινόμενον βοηθεῖν",
          "english_quote": "Its accusative form does not agree with τῷ ἐν εἱρκτῇ, and neither its attachment nor a contextually coherent contribution to the duty of assisting a prisoner is recoverable with confidence. The translation preserves its formal sense rather than silently replacing it, but no defensible contextual interpretation can presently be established.",
          "issue": "The note overlooks a defensible construction and consequently overstates the publication problem. The accusative participle can belong to the understood accusative subject of βοηθεῖν—the helper—rather than modifying the dative prisoner. On that analysis, the draft's literal passive wording, “while being sprinkled upon,” represents the supplied Greek without restoration. The intended significance of the sprinkling remains unexplained, but that uncertainty is not itself proof that no defensible English representation exists. The print is supplied as verified; no additional print verification is required merely because this expression is unusual.",
          "suggested_revision": "Rewrite the lexical and source-issue notes to explain the helper-subject analysis supporting the literal passive rendering. Preserve the formally possible middle alternative and explicitly state that the contextual significance of the sprinkling remains uncertain. Do not infer an object, identify the sprinkling with financial assistance, or emend the source without evidence. Replace the categorical publication block with a disclosure of this lexical and attachment uncertainty, and submit the revised passage and notes for fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "12.33",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
