      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὁμῶς τὸν τῆς φιλανθρωπίας ἐκθεμένου ἡμῖν λόγον",
          "english_quote": "The active genitive participle ἐκθεμένου has no explicitly stated genitive subject; Peter is readily supplied from the preceding speech, and λόγον functions as its object.",
          "issue": "The source-issue note misidentifies the participle's grammatical voice. ἐκθεμένου is a genitive singular aorist middle participle of ἐκτίθημι, not an active participle. Its middle form can nevertheless carry the sense “having set out” and take λόγον as its object. The contextual identification of Peter as its understood subject is defensible, and the main English does not require emendation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Change “active genitive participle” to “genitive singular aorist middle participle, here meaning ‘having set out.’” Retain the explanation of the understood subject and accusative object, along with the disclosure concerning printed ὁμῶς. Review the corrected notes afresh; this finding does not identify a corruption of the supplied print.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
